        <p class="profile-detail-region">Life · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Empress Dowager Cixi</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1835 CE – 1908 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">29 November 1835, probably in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, as Lady Yehe <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara">Nara</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> noblewoman of the Yehe Nara clan; daughter of Huizheng of the Bordered Blue Banner</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">15 November 1908 in the Hall of Graceful Bird at the Middle Sea, Zhongnanhai, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, a day after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangxu-emperor">Guangxu Emperor</a>; buried in the Eastern Ding Mausoleum</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Concubine of the Xianfeng Emperor (from 1852; Noble Consort Yi from 1857); Empress Dowager Cixi from 1861; regent for the Tongzhi Emperor from 1861 and for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangxu-emperor">Guangxu Emperor</a> from 1875; retired from regency 1889, resumed control 1898</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the Xinyou Coup of 1861 against the eight regents; the Tongzhi Restoration; the suppression of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days' Reform</a> in 1898; support for the Boxers and the war on the foreign powers in 1900; the New Policies after her return to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> in 1902; the contested reputation she has had since</span></div>
